ZyperOS: a frame the frontend will not show is left undrawn, the late skip
the Nintendo DS has (Diatom's RUN frameskip=late), from the same signal.

Diatom marks a frame it will not show: at 1x under frameskip=late, one that
starts more than half a period behind its schedule (two in a row at most),
and in fast forward the frames of a turn before its last. It says so through
libretro's audio buffer status callback, the underrun flag up for those
frames (diatom/src/env.c, diatom_env_frame_shown), and DSperate's wrapper
skips the DS's drawing on it (dsperate_frameskip). PPSSPP never asked for
the callback, so the PSP drew every frame however late it ran: on a GKD
Pixel 2 (1.1.0-rc.4) Tekken 6 at 0.62x its speed, Gran Turismo 0.50x,
WipEout Pure 0.47x, God of War 0.31x.

A new core option, ppsspp_frontend_frameskip ("Frameskip, when the frontend
asks for it", auto or disabled, auto by default, as dsperate_frameskip's
words), asks for the callback. A frame the emulation thread starts while the
flag is up runs with SKIPDRAW_SKIPFRAME, the bit PPSSPP's own frameskip sets:
its draws are left out, the game, its CPU and its sound run whole. The
undrawn frame's framebuffer is not really dirty, so __DisplayFlip asks for no
new frame and the frame after it runs in the same retro_run, drawn: never
two undrawn in a row, and that retro_run brings two periods of sound, which
Diatom (paced by sound for PPSSPP) waits two periods for. Not used with
PPSSPP's own Frameskip or Auto Frameskip on (the player's pick), nor with
duplicate frames on, whose 60 Hz flips would end a retro_run on the undrawn
frame. A frontend that never raises the flag (a game that keeps up, or a
frontend without frameskip=late) never has a frame skipped: every frame is
drawn, as before.

Measured on the Pixel 2 with a test core that skipped one frame in two
(fixed frameskip 1, the most this patch can skip): Tekken 6 0.62x to 1.00x,
Gran Turismo 0.50x to 0.73x, WipEout 0.47x to 0.76x, God of War 0.31x to
0.54x; PPSSPP's own auto frameskip (up to 2) skipped Daxter while it was on
time, 30 pictures a second down to 21.
diff --git a/libretro/libretro.cpp b/libretro/libretro.cpp
index e55ee9a..5d358fd 100644
--- a/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -129,6 +129,26 @@ namespace Libretro
    static bool detectVsyncSwapIntervalOptShown = true;
    static bool softwareRenderInitHack = false;
 
+   // The frontend's frame skip (ppsspp_frontend_frameskip, "auto"): through
+   // the audio buffer status callback the frontend says which frames it will
+   // not show - a frame that starts late (ZyperOS's Diatom under RUN
+   // frameskip=late) or one fast forward passes over - and its underrun flag
+   // is up for those. A frame the emulation thread starts while the flag is
+   // up has its drawing left out (SKIPDRAW_SKIPFRAME, as PPSSPP's own
+   // frameskip leaves it out); the game, its CPU and its sound run whole.
+   // A frame left undrawn does not end retro_run (its framebuffer is not
+   // really dirty: sceDisplay's __DisplayFlip asks for no new frame), so the
+   // frame after it runs in the same call and is drawn: never two undrawn in
+   // a row. A frontend that never raises the flag never has a frame skipped.
+   static bool frontendSkip = true;
+   static std::atomic<bool> frontendSkipBehind(false);
+
+   static void RETRO_CALLCONV frontend_skip_status(bool active, unsigned occupancy, bool underrun_likely)
+   {
+      (void)occupancy;
+      frontendSkipBehind.store(active && underrun_likely, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+   }
+
    static s64 expectedTimeUsPerRun = 0;
    static uint32_t vsyncSwapInterval = 1;
    static uint32_t vsyncSwapIntervalLast = 1;
@@ -766,6 +786,18 @@ static void check_variables(CoreParameter &coreParam)
          g_Config.bAutoFrameSkip = true;
    }
 
+   var.key = "ppsspp_frontend_frameskip";
+   if (environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_VARIABLE, &var) && var.value)
+      frontendSkip = strcmp(var.value, "disabled") != 0;
+   {
+      // Asked for on, given back off (NULL); the flag down until the
+      // frontend next says otherwise
+      struct retro_audio_buffer_status_callback cb = { frontend_skip_status };
+      if (!environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_AUDIO_BUFFER_STATUS_CALLBACK, frontendSkip ? &cb : NULL))
+         frontendSkip = false;
+      frontendSkipBehind.store(false, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+   }
+
    var.key = "ppsspp_frame_duplication";
    if (environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_VARIABLE, &var) && var.value)
    {
@@ -1395,6 +1427,14 @@ namespace Libretro
          gpu->BeginHostFrame(displayLayoutConfig);
       }
 
+      // The frontend's frame skip (frontend_skip_status): this frame
+      // undrawn while the frontend says it is behind. Not over PPSSPP's own
+      // frameskip, if the player picked it, nor with duplicate frames on,
+      // whose 60 Hz flips would end retro_run on the undrawn frame.
+      if (frontendSkip && frontendSkipBehind.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) &&
+          g_Config.iFrameSkip == 0 && !g_Config.bAutoFrameSkip && !g_Config.bRenderDuplicateFrames)
+         gstate_c.skipDrawReason |= SKIPDRAW_SKIPFRAME;
+
       PSP_RunLoopWhileState();
       switch (coreState) {
       case CORE_NEXTFRAME:
